## 3.3.4. EPR analysis and free radical capture experiment
It is reported that advanced oxidation technology based on sulfate system will produce ${\mathsf{S}}{\mathsf{O}}_{4}.^{-}$ , OH, $^{0_{2}.^{-},10_{2}}$ and other reactive oxygen species (ROS)[57], so electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) test is performed to detect the possible ROS (Fig. 9a-c). 5,5- dimethyl-1-pyrroline $N\mathrm{.}$ -oxide (DMPO) and 2,2,6,6- tetramethylpiperidine (TEMP) were used to capture the corresponding ROS in EPR test.Fig. 10..
No reactive oxygen species were produced when there was no catalyst involved (black line in Fig. 9a-c). After adding catalyst for $5\ \mathrm{min}$ , typical signal peaks of DMPO OH adducts with an intensity ratio of 1:2:2:1 are observed in Fig. 9a, that hyperfine coupling constants are $\mathsf{\Delta}\mathsf{z}_{\mathrm{N}}=\mathsf{\Delta}\mathsf{z}_{\mathrm{H}}=14.9\mathrm{~G~}$ [72], and the signals of $\mathrm{DMPO-SO_{4}.^{-}}$ adducts $\mathsf{\Omega}_{\cdot}\mathsf{\Omega}_{\mathsf{N}}=13.2\mathrm{\Omega}\mathrm{G}$ , $\mathfrak{A}_{\mathrm{H}}=9.6\mathrm{~G~}$ , $\mathsf{\Delta x_{H}}=1.48\mathrm{~G~}$ , and $\mathsf{\Delta}\mathsf{a}_{\mathrm{H}}=0.78\mathrm{~G})$ are distributed around it. Then, Fig. 9b shows the irregular strong signal of $\mathsf{D M P O-O_{2}\cdot^{-}}$ adducts. The three-line signals in the Fig. 9c indicates the existence of $\mathrm{TEMP}{-}^{1}0_{2}$ , which means that there are non-radical pathways in the PMS/catalyst system. In conclusion, $\mathrm{VCo-MOF@Ti_{3}C_{2}T_{x}}\mathrm{-}4$ can activate PMS to produce a variety of ROS, and multiple ROS cooperate to eliminate CIP through both radical and non-radical pathways.
In order to further clarify the role of various ROS in CIP removal in $\mathrm{PMS/VCo-MOF@Ti_{3}C_{2}T_{x}-4}$ system, quenching experiments were carried out with different ROS scavengers (Fig. 9d). ${}^{1}0_{2}$ , ${\mathsf{S}}{\mathsf{O}}_{4}.^{-}$ , OH and ${\mathsf{O}}_{2}{\cdot}^{-}{\mathsf{c a n}}$ be quenched with $\mathrm{~\boldmath~\cal~L~}$ -histidine, MeOH, tert-butyl alcohol (TBA) and 4-benzoquinone (BQ), respectively. Different from normal experimental results, the addition of MeOH only reduced the CIP removal efficiency by $12.6\%$ , while that of BQ was $35.9\%$ . In addition, the effects of TBA and L-histidine were also more significant than MeOH. The above experimental results indicates that ${\mathsf{S}}{\mathsf{O}}_{4}{\cdot}^{-}$ may be converted to OH and $\mathbf{O_{2}}\cdot\mathbf{\bar{\mu}}$ through the pathways shown in Eq. (8) - (10) [73]. The increase in the production of $0_{2}$  promotes the reaction path shown in Eq. (11) [74], and $^10_{2}$ produced by $0{_2}\cdot^{-}$ disproportionation enhances the non-radical pathway.
$\boldsymbol{0_{2}}\cdot\mathrm{\Sigma}^{-}$ participates in many important biogeochemical reactions and widely exists in the water environment [75]. Based on the abundant hydroxyl groups on the surface of MXene and the $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ formed after its oxidation, it is inferred that the hydrophilicity of the catalyst makes the adsorbed PMS easier to contact and react with $\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}$ , making the reaction more inclined to produce OH and $0_{2}\cdot^{-}$ . Previous studies have shown that the increase of $0_{2}$  formation rate will lead to the decrease of oxidant utilization, which is due to the fact that $\mathsf{O}_{2}.\mathsf{^{-}}$ is easy to form hydrogen bond in water and quickly disproportionated into $0_{2}$ and $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ [76]. However, the solid interface formed by the combination of MXene and MOF helps to inhibit disproportionation and improve the activity of $\boldsymbol{0_{2}}\cdot\mathrm{\Sigma}^{-}$ [77], and the shuttle electrons provided by $\boldsymbol{0_{2}}\cdot\mathrm{\Pi^{-}}$ are conducive to the circulation of ionic valence [62] and the removal of organic pollutants [78]. The results of quenching experiment also prove this view. In general, diversified ROS with high activity have made outstanding contributions to the $\mathrm{PMS/VCo-MOF@Ti_{3}C_{2}T_{x}-4}$ system.
