## 4. Conclusions
In this work, the in-situ growth of VCo-MOF on $\mathrm{Ti}_{3}\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{x}}$ lamella is realized, and new insights was provided for the origin of superoxide radicals produced by PMS activated by MXene composite catalysts. First, the hydrophilicity of $\mathrm{Ti}_{3}\mathrm{C}_{2}\mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{x}}$ and its excellent adsorption ability to PMS promotes the production of $\boldsymbol{0_{2}}\cdot\mathrm{\Pi^{-}}$ , and the surface of the composite catalyst improves the reactivity of $0_{2}\cdot^{-}$ , thus forming a special superoxide radical pathway. Secondly, the synergistic effect on the three transition metal active centers of the Ti-V-Co ternary system of the composite catalyst enhances its PMS activation performance. In addition, shuttle electrons are contributed by a variety of reactive oxygen species, including $0_{2}\cdot^{-}$ , which further improves the oxidation capacity of the system and the circulation rate of Ti (low valence) $/\mathrm{Ti}^{4+}$ , ${\mathsf{C o}}^{2+}/{\mathsf{C o}}^{3+}$ and $\mathsf{V}^{4+}/\mathsf{\Lambda}$ $\mathsf{V}^{5+}$ . In general, radical pathway $({\mathsf{S}}{\mathsf{O}}_{4}.^{-}$ , OH and $\mathsf{O}_{2}.\mathsf{^{-}}$ and nonradical pathway $(^{1}0_{2},\mathrm{~e~}^{-})$ cooperate to enhance the removal of CIP. Compared with the previous literature research results,
VCo-MOF with crystalline, uniform and good morphology was prepared in this paper, and its composites were to new fields with excellent performance.
In the future work, we will focus on optimization MOF@MXene DFT calculation model to get more accurate calculation results.
